      <img class="blog-hero-image" src="data:image/avif;base64," alt="MP Board 8th Class Result 2026 Declared">
      <div class="blog-body">
        <h1 class="blog-title">MP Board 8th Class Result 2026 DECLARED: Direct Links and How to Check Your Scorecard!</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">The much-awaited results for the Madhya Pradesh Board Class 8th examinations 2026 have been officially declared today, March 25, 2026! Students across the state can now access their scorecards and determine their academic standing. This blog post brings you all the crucial information, direct links, and a step-by-step guide to check your MP Board 8th Class Result 2026.</p>

        <p>The Rajya Shiksha Kendra, Madhya Pradesh (RSKMP) released the Class 5 and Class 8 results today, March 25, 2026. While initial reports indicated a release time of 11 AM or 11:30 AM, the results were ultimately announced at 1:30 PM. Over 20 lakh students appeared for these examinations, held from February 20 to February 28, 2026.</p>

        <h2 class="section-title">Where to Check Your MP Board 8th Result 2026?</h2>
        <p>Students can primarily check their results on the official website of Rajya Shiksha Kendra, Madhya Pradesh. Additionally, other official portals may also host the results.</p>

        <div class="benefit-card">
          <p>✅ <strong>Official Website:</strong> <a href="https://rskmp.in/" target="_blank">rskmp.in</a></p>
          <p>✅ <strong>Other Potential Websites:</strong> mpresults.nic.in, mpbse.nic.in</p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="section-title">How to Check MP Board 8th Class Result 2026 Online: Step-by-Step Guide</h2>
        <p>Follow these simple steps to access your MP Board Class 8th scorecard online:</p>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">1. Visit the Official Website</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">Go to the official Rajya Shiksha Kendra, Madhya Pradesh website: <a href="https://rskmp.in/" target="_blank">rskmp.in</a>.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">2. Locate the Result Link</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">On the homepage, look for the "Class 8th Result 2026" link. Click on it.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">3. Enter Your Credentials</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">You will be prompted to enter your Roll Number or Samagra ID. Ensure you enter the correct details as mentioned on your admit card. You will also need to enter a Captcha Code.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">4. View Your Result</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">After entering the details, click on the "Submit" button. Your MP Board 8th Class Result 2026 will be displayed on the screen.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">5. Download and Print</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">Download your scorecard and take a printout for future reference. It's advisable to have multiple copies.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="highlight-text">
          <strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Due to high traffic, the websites might experience slowdowns. Keep your Roll Number or Samagra ID ready and try accessing the link a few times if you face issues.
        </div>

        <h2 class="section-title">Details Mentioned on Your MP Board 8th Class Marksheet</h2>
        <p>Your online marksheet will contain several important pieces of information. It's crucial to verify all the details carefully.</p>
        <div class="benefit-card">
          <p>✅ Student's Name</p>
          <p>✅ Roll Number</p>
          <p>✅ Subject Name</p>
          <p>✅ Subject-wise Marks</p>
          <p>✅ Total Marks Obtained</p>
          <p>✅ Grades</p>
          <p>✅ Result Status (Pass/Fail)</p>
          <p>✅ Division</p>
          <p>✅ Father's Name</p>
          <p>✅ Mother's Name</p>
        </div>
        <p>If you find any discrepancies, report them to your school officials immediately.</p>

        <h2 class="section-title">MP Board 8th Class Passing Marks 2026</h2>
        <p>To successfully pass the MP Board Class 8th examination, students are required to secure a minimum of 33 marks out of 100 in each subject. Additionally, an overall aggregate of 33% is mandatory.</p>

        <h2 class="section-title">Previous Year's Performance and Trends</h2>
        <p>Understanding previous years' trends can provide some context for the current results. The MP Board has consistently seen high pass percentages for Class 8. In 2025, the overall pass percentage for Class 8 was 90.02%, a significant improvement from 87.71% in 2024. Girls have notably outperformed boys in both Class 5 and Class 8 in recent years.</p>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">MP Board Class 8 Pass Percentage Trend</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">
            <table>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Year</th>
                  <th>Overall Pass Percentage (Class 8)</th>
                  <th>Girls Pass Percentage (Class 8)</th>
                  <th>Boys Pass Percentage (Class 8)</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td>2025</td>
                  <td>90.02%</td>
                  <td>91.72%</td>
                  <td>88.41%</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>2024</td>
                  <td>87.71%</td>
                  <td>89.56%</td>
                  <td>85.94%</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
            <p class="mt-3">These figures set a high benchmark for the 2026 results.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="section-title">Re-totalling of Marks</h2>
        <p>For students who are not satisfied with their results, the Madhya Pradesh Rajya Shiksha Kendra (RSKMP) will open an application window for re-totalling of marks. This facility will allow students to request a re-check of their scores within a specified deadline.</p>

        <h2 class="section-title">What's Next?</h2>
        <p>Congratulations to all the students who have successfully cleared their MP Board Class 8th examinations! For those who may not have achieved the desired results, remember that there are always opportunities for improvement, including supplementary exams.</p>
        <p>Stay tuned to the official RSKMP website for any further announcements regarding re-totalling applications or supplementary examination schedules. Your hard work has paid off, and this is just another step in your academic journey!</p>
      </div>
